# {{ .name }}

.NET extractor integration. One run = one sweep: the framework runner lists
the inbound port, runs each file through the Intropy extractor pipeline,
publishes the result as a CloudEvent to the `{{ .channel }}` topic on the Dapr
pub/sub, deletes the source file, and exits. Scheduling is deployment
configuration (a Kubernetes CronJob in production); locally the system host
runs the block once at startup.

## What this project contains

Only business code:

| File | What it holds |
|---|---|
| `src/{{ .componentClass }}.cs` | The rules: idempotency key and version, output event subject and time, incident identity |
| `src/Process/` | The pipeline steps: `Deserializer`, `Validator`, `Transformer` |
| `src/Model/` | The source file shape (`Source{{ .payloadType }}`) |
| `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Unit/` | Step unit tests |

Everything else is supplied:

- **By `Intropy.Framework.ExtractorHost`** (the one package reference): the
  entry point, the sweep, Dapr, the platform-service clients, telemetry, and
  the 0/1/2 exit codes.
- **By the system topology**, through `INTROPY__CONFIG`: the component name
  (`{{ .appId }}`), the organization, the CloudEvent source
  (`urn:<organization>:{{ .appId }}` unless the topology overrides it), the
  published message (`{{ .publishes }}`, also the CloudEvents type), the source
  port's binding (`{{ .port }}`), and the platform-service app ids.

## How a run flows

```
scheduled run (CronJob / host)
   │
   ▼
sweep inbound port ──▶ per file:
   │
   ▼
read ──▶ deserialize ──▶ validate ──▶ idempotency check ──▶ transform
   │
   ▼
publish CloudEvent to '{{ .channel }}'
   │
   ▼
delete source file ──▶ next file
   │
   ▼
exit 0
```

Off the happy path: duplicates cancel without publishing, business failures
route an incident (and both consume the file), a technical failure keeps the
file for the next run and fails the run with exit 1.
{{- if .empty }}

Every step body and rule throws `NotImplementedException` — this project was
scaffolded with empty bodies for a migration agent to fill in. The step tests
fail until the steps are implemented.
{{- end }}

## Build and test

```bash
task build
task test
```

The extractor does not run standalone. It runs via its system host, which
runs it once at startup and provides the source binding, pub/sub, platform
services, and the runtime identity.

## Shared contracts

The canonical payload type (`{{ .payloadType }}`) lives in the sibling
`../{{ .contracts }}` project, referenced from `src/{{ .name }}.csproj`; the
consuming loader deserializes exactly that record.

## Container image

```bash
docker build --build-context contracts=../{{ .contracts }} -t {{ .appId }} .
```

Multi-stage build on the .NET 10 chiseled runtime. The shared contracts sibling
enters the build as the `contracts` named context. The image contains only the
app — the Dapr sidecar, components, and runtime identity come from the
deployment environment.
